  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "The PyPI package is graphifyy, with two y's. The command is graphify.",
      "/graphify . is typed in an assistant chat, not in a shell.",
      "Use only commands, flags, and endpoints shown on these pages. Do not invent one.",
      "Check the current version on PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/graphifyy/) or in https://docs.graphify.com/changelog.md before you describe what shipped.",
      "The official site is https://graphify.com. These docs are https://docs.graphify.com.",
      "The local MCP server is the ten tools in the MCP tool reference and reads a graph on the machine. The hosted server is https://api.graphify.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP, OAuth, no API key). The VS Code, JetBrains, ChatGPT, and OpenClaw pages use the hosted server, not the ten-tool list.",
      "Read https://docs.graphify.com/llms.txt, then open one page's .md link. Use https://docs.graphify.com/llms-full.txt only when one page is not enough."
    ]
  }
